# Sky time and world events

Requested 2026-11-07 after testing the sky-color comparison.
Research: [time, Seven Signs and cursed-weapon findings](docs/NATIVE_SKY_TIME_EVENTS.md).

- [x] Research whether the color rows represent time of day. Original tables
  contain T=0..24 keys and comments for night, dawn, morning, midday and sunset.
- [x] Identify the four source presets: default (0), Dusk (1), Dawn (2),
  cursed sword (3), from the original EnvType declarations and Korean comments.
- [x] Research world events. Historical Seven Signs notes describe Dawn's
  violet sky/solar eclipse and Dusk's green sky/eye in the moon. Cursed-weapon
  drops cause a brief world effect; Interlude emulator code sends ExRedSky(10).
- [x] Check moon-phase evidence. Moon color/scale are time-keyed; an ordinary
  waxing/waning calendar is not established. Keep that question open.

Implementation and remaining research:

- [ ] Confirm the pinned native client's ClientSetTime, SSQInfo and ExRedSky
  consumers: time units, environment selection, duration units and restoration.
  The source comments and public emulator agree on intended roles; the exact
  packet-to-timeenv mapping still needs client evidence.
- [ ] Establish native table consumption/interpolation, T=24 midnight wrap and
  transition behavior. Resolve timeenv3 SkyBoxColor NUM=1 versus 25 physical
  rows and duplicate HSVTerrainLight sections before choosing a loader policy.
- [ ] Implement ordinary accelerated game time with an explicit offline clock
  input and a future server-time input. Interlude emulator reference: rate 6,
  one game day per four real hours. Keep local wall time separate from game time.
- [ ] Keep Seven Signs environment state separate from time of day. Support
  normal/competition, Dawn validation, Dusk validation and validation-end reset;
  retain the current event state when entering the world.
- [ ] Implement the temporary cursed-weapon sky effect separately. Verify
  overlap/retrigger rules, event priority and restoration to the underlying
  Seven Signs state at the current game time, rather than a fixed daytime row.
- [ ] Identify and integrate original sun, moon, stars and eclipse/eye assets,
  visibility, movement, color and scale. Investigate any additional lunar-phase
  driver before adding a lunar calendar.
- [ ] Verify dawn/dusk/night/noon and midnight continuity, Seven Signs changes,
  entry during an event, cursed-weapon effect start/end and overlapping effects
  on both source and authored routes, desktop and mobile. Preserve authored
  materials and terrain data; keep the literal-row comparison available.
